requirements:
Specifies strict dimensional limits across nominal shank diameters (1.6 to 9.6 mm) for five key head parameters:
a) Head Diameter (D): ranges from 3.2 ±0.15 mm (for d=1.6) to 19.0 ±0.9 mm (for d=9.6);
b) Head Height (E): ranges from 0.7 mm (for d=1.6) to 4.1 mm (for d=9.6);
c) Head Side Flat (F): ranges from 0.4 mm (for d=1.6) to 2.4 mm (for d=9.6);
d) Crown Radius (G): ranges from 1.4 mm (for d=1.6) to 8.3 mm (for d=9.6);
e) Edge Radius r (Reference only): ranges from 0.15 mm to 0.25 mm.

To prevent metallurgical mix-ups on the assembly floor, rivets must be physically marked on the head or on the end of the shank with indented symbols:
a) Alloy No. 1: Two indented circular dots (maximum diameter of 0.8 mm);
b) Alloy No. 2: Two indented circular dots with a curved line or dash.
